### M11 — Workspaces, rules, Work Records and timers (`accepted` contract 2026-10-02; slices 1–9 implemented; the renames remain)

Goal: what the model is given and what it leaves behind are scoped to the place the work happens in. A Workspace is an Emacs project with its rules (`AGENTS.md`), its conversations and its Work Records; nothing applies everywhere; work that has to outlive a Run has a record the model registers through tools and the product keeps, schedules and closes without parsing the answer. The contract is [the workspace record](decisions/accepted/2026-10-01-workspace-work-record-session-rules.md) (rules W1–W11, S1–S3, R1–R5, K1–K14, T1–T4); what Holon, Codex, Antigravity, jj and Emacs do is in [the reference facts](research/workspace-and-work-record-references.md). It came out of the goals batch of 2026-10-01 (`.scratch/task-sim/GOALS-BATCH-REPORT.md`), where the personal-agent tasks failed: a stated preference did not survive a restart (0 of 3) and reminders were unreliable (1 of 3).

Each slice gets its own decision record before code, red tests first, and real-task runs for acceptance. The order is the leader's recommendation.

